\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Estimation bias against decision regret for every level (\% of the baseline operating cost). Loss-aware levels lie on the \mbox  {bias\,$=$\,regret} diagonal, so a model's estimate predicts what its schedule costs to run; the inset magnifies that cluster near the origin (CP+L$_b$ coincides with CP+L, and L6 with L3). The loss-blind copperplate and topology-only control (CP, ND$^0$) sit far above the diagonal: a small negative bias but a large positive regret, i.e.\ cheap on paper yet expensive to execute.}}{20}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:regret}{{5}{20}{Estimation bias against decision regret for every level (\% of the baseline operating cost). Loss-aware levels lie on the \mbox {bias\,$=$\,regret} diagonal, so a model's estimate predicts what its schedule costs to run; the inset magnifies that cluster near the origin (CP+L$_b$ coincides with CP+L, and L6 with L3). The loss-blind copperplate and topology-only control (CP, ND$^0$) sit far above the diagonal: a small negative bias but a large positive regret, i.e.\ cheap on paper yet expensive to execute}{figure.5}{}}
