\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Drift of a frozen loss adder against trunk pipe length across the 135 synthetic networks. An adder calibrated on any one network mis-estimates the loss burden on others by a mean of 23.5 and up to 40.1 percentage points of cost, which is why the node-resolved model, computing the loss endogenously, is the transferable one.}}{25}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:drift}{{7}{25}{Drift of a frozen loss adder against trunk pipe length across the 135 synthetic networks. An adder calibrated on any one network mis-estimates the loss burden on others by a mean of 23.5 and up to 40.1 percentage points of cost, which is why the node-resolved model, computing the loss endogenously, is the transferable one}{figure.7}{}}
